cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this method, data or code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GeoFuego Harmonization: MODIS to VIIRS-equivalent harmonized fire-hotspot calendar for Argentina, 2000 to 2025 (NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026)"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-14"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24220107"
url: "https://spaceapps.geofuego.com.ar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/germankovacevic-lab/geofuego-harmonization"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/germankovacevic-lab/geofuego-harmonization/blob/main/LICENSE"
authors:
  - family-names: Kovacevic
    given-names: "Germán Ricardo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4270-1963"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Buenos Aires, Argentina (GeoFuego.com.ar)"
keywords: [MODIS, VIIRS, FIRMS, active fire, hotspot harmonization, fire calendar, Argentina, NASA Space Apps 2026, CONAE]
abstract: "One consistent monthly fire-hotspot calendar for Argentina, November 2000 to December 2025, from NASA FIRMS MODIS (Terra, Aqua) and VIIRS (S-NPP) active-fire detections: MODIS counts converted to VIIRS-equivalent counts with a conversion factor per 0.25 degree cell, calendar month and satellite set, fitted on paired days of the 2012-2023 overlap with hierarchical shrinkage, a separate static-source class (gas flares, industry), satellite-outage gap filling, and an 80 % prediction interval calibrated out of sample and tested on 2024-2025. Includes a bridge S-NPP to NOAA-20/NOAA-21 for the live series and a static web app (area of interest, date range, calendar, CSV/PNG). Code written with SI assistance (Claude, Anthropic); reviewed and validated by the team. Code is MIT; data products and figures are CC BY 4.0. Input data: NASA FIRMS (MODIS Collection 6/6.1 MCD14ML country archives; VIIRS VNP14IMG S-NPP, VJ114IMG NOAA-20, VJ214IMG NOAA-21), ERA5 monthly cloud fraction and precipitation (Copernicus Climate Change Service, CDS; contains modified Copernicus Climate Change Service information 2026), NOAA CPC ONI, GWIS/JRC MCD64A1 country tables, IGN Argentina. Licences of all inputs are listed in README (Data sources and licences)."
